simplescreenshot (1.0.3-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: install the toolbar icon font (assets/iconfont.ttf, family
    "icon") as a system font under /usr/share/fonts/truetype/simplescreenshot
    and refresh the fontconfig cache in postinst/postrm. A long-running
    instance can lose sight of the per-process app-font registration when
    the system font environment changes under it (e.g. another package's
    upgrade regenerating fontconfig caches), which made toolbar icons render
    as random CJK/tofu glyphs until restart; the fontconfig-visible system
    copy survives that churn. The bundled assets copy is still registered
    per-process as a fallback and remains the source for development runs.

 -- xinwf <xinwf18@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Nov 2026 01:05:00 +0800

simplescreenshot (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Long screenshot: capture a frame only once the pixels have settled
    (two identical snapshots in a row), so frames grabbed mid smooth-scroll
    no longer produce duplicated ("ghost") bands.
  * Long screenshot: reject frames whose best match is not a real overlap
    instead of painting a misaligned band into the result.
  * Tray: dismiss the popup menu and let the compositor repaint before the
    capture overlay starts, so the menu no longer ends up in screenshots
    taken from the tray menu (capture and delayed capture items).
  * Tray: detect a legacy XEmbed systray host (_NET_SYSTEM_TRAY_S<n>) at
    startup and prefer GtkStatusIcon there — left click captures, right
    click opens the menu. GNOME Shell owns no such selection and keeps
    using the AppIndicator path, where middle click captures instead.
  * About panel: show the project repository URL below the author line.
  * Pin window: fix dragging the pinned image to another position.
  * Pin window: draw a soft shadow around the pinned screenshot so it
    visually stands out from the desktop content behind it.
  * Documentation: fix config.json key names and the table of contents
    in README; man page documents all --enter modes (long / video /
    ocr / qr / pin) and Wayland/XWayland support; UI language is
    Chinese / English only.
  * prerm: use pkill -x instead of killall in the maintainer script
    (lintian killall-is-dangerous); build is warning-free again
    (vendored nlohmann/json headers are included as system headers).
  * Version 1.0.3.

 -- xinwf <xinwf18@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0800

simplescreenshot (1.0.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Screen recording rework:
    - GIF: record an intermediate MP4 first and assemble the GIF after
      stop. A live palettegen filter graph produced an empty file when
      ffmpeg was quit via the 'q' key (reproducible on ffmpeg >= 6).
    - Audio: capture via a feeder process (pw-cat on PipeWire desktops,
      parecord on PulseAudio) writing a WAV file that is mixed onto the
      video at stop — ffmpeg's pulse monitor input records silence
      through pipewire-pulse. The speaker and microphone toggles now
      take effect; enabling both mixes the two sources.
    - Check ffmpeg when recording starts and verify the encoded file
      after stop: missing dependency and failed encodes now show a
      dialog instead of silently producing broken files.
  * Fix segfault when closing capture toolbars (reproducible on the
    recording bar): hover tracking pointed into freed widget trees.
    Tool windows are now hidden immediately and destroyed on the next
    idle, outside their own GTK signal handlers.
  * Fix the recording elapsed timer freezing at 00:01 (one-shot timer
    was never re-armed).
  * Packaging: tesseract-ocr / tesseract-ocr-chi-sim move from Depends
    to Recommends alongside ffmpeg and xclip. QR decoding stays fully
    bundled (quirc). Each optional feature checks its helper at use
    time and shows a missing-dependency dialog.

 -- xinwf <xinwf18@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:10:00 +0800

simplescreenshot (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 1.0.0 public release.
  * OCR: bundled RapidOCR python plugin (assets/plugins/ocr_rapidocr.py)
    with automatic tesseract fallback; startup hint when RapidOCR is not
    installed (dismissable, stored as ocr.rapidocrHintHidden). Custom OCR
    plugin path can be set via config.json (ocr.plugin).
  * Delay-capture dialog is now a WM-managed window: draggable by its
    title area and coverable by other windows (no longer always-on-top).

 -- xinwf <xinwf18@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:20:00 +0800
